[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Make a package with no description fail rather than vanish from the README

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-README-ROWS-FOLLOW-DESCRIPTIONS-NOT-PACKAGES
TITLE: Make a package with no description fail rather than vanish from the README
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
dev/generate.nix's mkDescriptionRows maps over dev/data.nix's description
attrsets, not over the overlay's package set, so a package with no description
entry is silently absent from the generated README table. Nothing fails: not
the generator, not nix flake check, not the drift check, which compares the
generated file against the same incomplete input.

Fix shape: derive the row set from the overlay group and look each description
up, so a missing one throws with the package's name. That inverts the failure
from a silent omission into an eval error naming exactly what to write.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Found while landing SLICE-STRICTDOC-OVERLAY: the package was registered in
overlays/default.nix, config.update.targets and the cache-hit-parity registry
-- three surfaces that DO fail when incomplete -- and would still have shipped
absent from the public README, because the fourth surface is a lookup table
nothing cross-checks. The three loud registries are why this was caught at all,
and they are the model for the fix.

Not scoped to this plan's subject. Recorded here because it was found here and
there is no other parking lot; move it if the repo grows one.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Filed as issue #1266, self-contained, on 2026-08-25 -- the parking lot the
rationale above asks for. That issue is the user-visible tracker; this node is
the design-graph record of which slice found it. Close both together.
<<<
